Subject: [PATCH 16/22] feat(matcher): a hotel is hospitality, Kobuleti is in
 Adjara (1699 part 3, A16)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The board's example — a goal „hotel in Kobuleti" against an offer
„hospitality in Adjara" — is now one sure match. fieldPlaces.ts holds two
small maps: field families (hospitality, tourism, logistics, customs, real
estate, marketing, investment, healthcare; Georgian and Latin) and Georgia's
regions with their main towns. The matcher reads field and place apart: the
goal must speak of the offer's field or its family, and be where the offer
is — the town it names, or any town of the region it names. A goal naming no
place is not sure for an offer that names one (D498).

This also closes a part-1 gap: the whole field line was read as field words,
so „a lawyer in Batumi" matched „hospitality in Batumi" on the city alone.
Server only; offers stay empty until §109, so nothing changes live until then.

